# arm - talk to the servos on the wall.
#
# This is the slice P0 needs: the Feetech bus, calibration, and the lerobot-*
# CLIs that `pinkrab` wraps.
#
# LeRobot is pinned to an exact release rather than a range. Its CLI argument
# shapes and the directory it keeps calibration in are part of this project's
# contract - pinkrab_core builds `--robot.left_arm_config.port=...` strings and
# reads back `calibration/robots/pinkrab_follower/<id>.json`. A minor bump can move
# either without breaking anything that looks like an API.
#
# Requires Python >= 3.12 (lerobot's own floor).
lerobot[diffusion,feetech,placo-dep,scipy-dep,smolvla,training]==0.6.1

# placo is not optional on this rig. With no leader arm there is no joint-space
# copy, so everything that moves these arms solves inverse kinematics, and
# lerobot.model.kinematics refuses to load without it.

# scipy is not optional either, though lerobot leaves it to an extra. Importing
# lerobot.policies pulls in pi0_fast, which imports scipy.fftpack at module level,
# so any lerobot-* command fails without it. The extra pins a numpy 2 build; a
# venv with --system-site-packages otherwise falls through to the distribution's
# scipy, which is compiled against numpy 1 and raises a dtype size mismatch.

# diffusion brings diffusers, which Diffusion Policy needs to train and to run:
# its noise scheduler denoises every chunk at inference too.

# smolvla brings transformers, which SmolVLA needs to run, not only to train, so it
# is here rather than in a training slice.

# training brings the dataset side - datasets, pyarrow, torchcodec - that
# `pinkrab-umi convert` writes with and lerobot-train reads with, and a venv
# built from this lock alone cannot do either without it.

# ruckig shapes a policy's commands in the safety gate: the quickest trajectory
# to each command that keeps a joint's speed, acceleration and jerk under their
# limits, worked out every tick. A wheel with no dependencies of its own.
ruckig==0.19.4

# setuptools stays below 80: from 80 on `setup.py develop` no longer takes
# --editable, which colcon passes to every Python package on a
# `colcon build --symlink-install`, so the workspace would only build as copies.
setuptools<80
